.org/www-project-web-security-testing-guide/v41/4-Web_Application_Security_Testing/07-Input_Validation_Testing/18-Testing_for_Server_Side_Template_Injection)\n - [https://portswigger.net/research/server-side-template-injection](https://portswigger.net/research/server-side-template-injection)\n","text":"The application might dynamically evaluate untrusted input, which can lead to a code injection vulnerability. An attacker can execute arbitrary code, potentially gaining complete control of the system. To prevent this vulnerability, avoid executing code containing user input. If this is unavoidable, validate and sanitize the input, and use safe alternatives for evaluating user input."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/java.thymeleaf.thymeleaf-template-injection.thymeleaf-template-injection","id":"java.thymeleaf.thymeleaf-template-injection.thymeleaf-template-injection","name":"java.thymeleaf.thymeleaf-template-injection.thymeleaf-template-injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: java.thymeleaf.thymeleaf-template-injection.thymeleaf-template-injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected an HTTP request sent via HttpGet. This could lead to sensitive information being sent  over an insecure channel. Instead, it is recommended to send requests over HTTPS."},"help":{"markdown":"Detected an HTTP request sent via HttpGet. This could lead to sensitive information being sent  over an insecure channel. Instead, it is recommended to send requests over HTTPS.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/problem-based-packs.insecure-transport.java-stdlib.httpget-http-request.httpget-http-request)\n - [https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/11/docs/api/java.base/java/net/URLConnection.html](https://docs.